  <title id="bdl19bmaapproximations-title">Finite approximations to the Bayesian model average</title>
  <desc id="bdl19bmaapproximations-desc">Three stacked panels share a horizontal parameter axis w. Top: a multimodal posterior p(w given D) with seven sharp peaks. Four large filled markers sit on top of four separated peaks (deep ensembles); three small filled markers sit close together on one peak (VI); small hollow markers are spread around each of the four marked peaks (Multi-SWAG). Dashed vertical lines drop from every marker to the axis. Middle: the predictive p(y given w) for one test input, low and wiggly over the two left modes, higher over the central modes and slightly lower again on the right. Bottom: the discrepancy dist(p, q) as a function of the location of one additional evaluation; it is high over the two left modes and the right mode and dips to its minimum around the already represented mode labeled w hat. A legend names the three marker types.</desc>
